# Scraper

## Allowlist

- Support only an explicit, small allowlist of sites.
- Route via `dispatch.py` (site → parser lookup). Do not scrape arbitrary hosts.

## Fetch / parse rules

- Scrape **only** the given URL. Never follow links found on the page.
- Use `httpx` (async) + BeautifulSoup with `lxml`.

## Site parsers (`scraper/sites/`)

- One `*_site.py` module per site. Shared types live in `models.py`; allowlist registration lives in `registry.py`. Keep `__init__.py` empty of code (docstring only).
- Expected shape: HTML → job-fields matching `jobs` sheet columns (`job_title`, `job_description`, `job_location`, `job_company`, `job_salary`, `job_type`, `job_posted_date`, etc.).
- Each `*_site` module exports `SITE_HOST` (hostname, lowercase, no `www.`) or `SITE_HOSTS`, and `parse`; `registry.py` auto-registers only modules whose name ends with `_site` into `SITE_ALLOWLIST`. No manual dispatch edit.
